{{#if isRest}}---
description: REST Controller Implementation Guidelines
globs: "**/*.controller.ts"
alwaysApply: true
---
- Use proper HTTP decorators: @Get(), @Post(), @Put(), @Delete(), @Patch()
- Apply DTOs for request validation using class-validator
- Use proper HTTP status codes and response formats
- Handle errors properly and return appropriate HTTP status codes
- Apply Swagger decorators for API documentation:
  ```ts
  @ApiOperation({ summary: 'Create a new user' })
  @ApiResponse({ status: 201, type: UserDto })
  ```
- Follow RESTful URL patterns: /users, /users/:id, etc.
- Validate request bodies and query parameters using DTOs
- Delegate business logic to services, controllers should be thin
@controller-template.ts{{/if}}
